# Completion review — add-model-benchmark-search

**Status:** the search-route, queue-liveness, and durable rate-limit recovery
fixes are implemented. Focused verification and independent review pass. PR,
deployment, and controlled live acceptance remain pending.

## Root cause

The original scheduled queue called the low-level search handler as
`duckduckgo-free` with empty credentials. A live inspection then found 45
`duckduckgoFree:error` receipts in the latest 100 stored runs, and direct
DuckDuckGo requests timed out from the host. The shared credential-resolving
`ollama-search` route fix is now on the deployed `dbb02d7` image; the queue
liveness and complete-miss gating fixes in this branch are not deployed.
Source review also found that a complete exact AA/official match with no usable
fitness could still reach HF/web discovery; the current branch blocks that
search and finishes the row review-required.

## Live queue incident (2026-10-26)

Live inspection found 20 runs all `running`, each claimed at 17:02:47Z with
attempt 2; queue counts and timestamps had not moved, and there were no
matching search or benchmark logs. Source confirms the old drain claimed 20
rows before processing and saved their outcomes only after the whole batch.
This explains why one slow row could leave the whole batch stuck. The exact
awaited operation for the live stall is not proven from available logs.

## Fix

- Route scheduled discovery through the shared credential-resolving search
  executor and explicitly select `ollama-search`, which resolves its key from
  the active `ollama-cloud` connection.
- Stop before the request unless its registry cost is zero. Reject any result
  whose provider ID changes or whose reported search cost is nonzero.
- Leave search alternates unset. Search results remain review-required, and
  strict-SO extraction remains pinned to the existing exact free connection.
- Materialize exact AA/leaderboard evidence for up to 20 eligible rows without
  claiming them, recompute cohort scores once, then claim and finish one row at
  a time. Save HF/search evidence before strict-SO, abort strict-SO after five
  minutes, and schedule fresh `running` recovery at its 15-minute stale edge.
- Require an exact miss across AA and every official source before HF or web
  search. Exact known-source matches without usable fitness finish
  review-required without consuming discovery-search quota.

## Verification

- RED reproduced the missing `validateOllamaSearchResponse` guard and the
  exact-match search-boundary violation. Queue-level failure coverage verifies
  an Ollama HTTP error records `source_error`, saves no evidence, and sends no
  strict-SO request. The focused suite passes 34/34,
  including one-row claims, timeout evidence preservation, stale recovery, and
  max-attempt cleanup before source loading.
- `npm run check:docs-all` exits 0; it reports 98 existing potential-drift
  warnings. Prettier and `git diff --check` pass for all changed files.
- `npm run typecheck:core` exits 2 with 757 TypeScript errors in unrelated
  project files. It reports no diagnostics for either changed TypeScript file.
- Code Simplifier applied to the owned source and test changes.
- Independent Luna-xhigh review confirmed the credential mapping, exact
  zero-cost provider pin, no-alternate behavior, and unchanged strict-SO path.
  The liveness review found one mismatch for max-attempt cleanup; the new
  regression reproduced it, and the fix now runs terminal cleanup before
  eligibility checks. Follow-up review confirmed that correction and found no
  remaining findings. A second focused follow-up verified exact-match, incomplete
  scan, and complete-miss gates; no findings remain.

